VAL_ 392 GEAR_SHIFTER 1 "P" 2 "R" 4 "N" 8 "D" ;
VAL_ 392 GEAR 26 "S" 4 "D" 3 "N" 2 "R" 1 "P" ;

CM_ SG_ 392 GEAR_SHIFTER "One-hot lever position: P=1, R=2, N=4, D=8. Raw 0 is AMBIGUOUS --
it means BOTH Sport AND the lever passing BETWEEN detents, confirmed by the owner of a 2015
Accord (HONDA_ELESYS). That is why 0 has no VAL entry here: a decoder that maps it straight
to Sport emits a phantom Sport on every single shift. Measured over 473k frames, every 0 run
in that recording was a transient -- 47 of them, median 3 frames (30 ms), max 520 ms, all
below 0.5 m/s -- because Sport was never selected during it. Only DURATION separates the two
cases, so carstate.py resolves it with a 1.0 s dwell (see update_gear_elesys). GEAR (36|5) is
documented as carrying 26 for Sport and is used as a fast path, but that value has never been
observed on this car, so the dwell is what is actually relied on.";

CM_ SG_ 401 CVT_UNKNOWN_1 "Probably measured/actual CVT ratio";
CM_ SG_ 401 CVT_UNKNOWN_2 "Probably target/commanded CVT ratio";
VAL_ 401 GEAR_SHIFTER 1 "P" 2 "R" 3 "N" 4 "D" 7 "L" 10 "S";
